# Copy to .env.local. Vite exposes only VITE_-prefixed variables to the client.

# The FastAPI hair-AI service (services/ai): POST /analyze reads the photo,
# POST /generate renders the chosen style onto it. Start it with
# `python main.py` in services/ai.
#
# Relative, like the API below: Vite proxies `/ai` to the service, so the
# browser never names its host and CORS never comes into it. A deployment sets
# an absolute URL here and lists this app's origin in the service's
# CORS_ORIGINS.
VITE_AI_API_URL=/ai

# The Django backend (services/backend).
#
# A RELATIVE path on purpose. In development Vite proxies `/api` to Django
# (see `server.proxy` in vite.config.ts), so the browser asks whatever origin
# it loaded the page from — which is what lets a phone on the same wifi work
# without any address being written down anywhere. An absolute URL here would
# name a host the phone cannot reach, and would go stale every time DHCP
# changed it.
#
# A real deployment sets this to its own API origin at build time, e.g.
# https://api.gosalon.com/api — the proxy serves `vite dev` and `vite preview`
# and has no part in a production bundle.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# The rest of the app (bookings, the catalogue, the provider screens) still
# answers from src/mockData.
VITE_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
